    "created_at": "2024-09-27T20:59:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-09-27T20:59:32Z",
    "body": "I don't think we will ever be able to make all URLs valid URL patterns (or, if they're valid, have the same meaning), though we can make needing escaping a little less common. I agree that describing how to effectively escape (either by hand or programmatically) would be a useful addition (I've written such algorithms myself, and they are indeed not trivial).\r\n\r\nI think it's _probably_ possible to allow other-modifier tokens (`+` and `?`) after some fixed text to get subsumed by it, since it otherwise has no existing syntactic meaning. This would make things like `web+foo` viable without changing the meaning of `:foo?` and similar. It's not completely trivial to make this change, though, so I need to actually try to make the change for that to work.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
